  "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100085/assets/14b4aa0c290ef70b8442c5e5176c3311f9968b7a774b52a6a2472c356f190866.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,4\\le x\\le 8,\\,2\\sqrt{x-4}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{2x}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dA & ={\\int }_{4}^{8}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x-4}}^{\\sqrt{2x}}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
